Using BST tree properties - O(h) Time and O(1) SpaceWe begin traversal from root. For every node, we need to take care of 3 cases for to find its inorder successor.Right child of node is not NULL : . The successor will be the leftmost node in its right subtree. For example, successor for 1 is 3The node is the Rightmost in Tree : The successor is NULL. For example, node 6 in the above diagram.If right child of the node is NULL :. The successor must be an ancestor. Travel up using the parent pointer until we see a node which is left child of its parent. The parent of such a node is the successor.Please refer to Inorder Successor in Binary Search Tree for implementation.
